      "brief": "# Brief: Reader D: Sarbanes-Oxley & the PCAOB (Phase 2)\n\nFollow `00-common-rules.md`. Card ids `S-001`… in `work/facts/reader-sox.json`. No web. Target: 50–80 cards.\n\n**Purpose:** fact cards for the new page \"Why This Matters to You\". For each provision below, card three things: (a) **what the law requires**, from the statute text; (b) **the problem Congress had in mind**, from the committee reports, CRS summary, and testimony, especially where they cite Enron; (c) **how the SEC or PCAOB first put it in place** (2002–2003), where the library covers it.\n\n**Provisions:** §§101–109 (the PCAOB); §§201 (services outside the scope of practice), 202, 203 (partner rotation), 204, 206 (conflicts of interest / \"cooling off\"); §302 (CEO/CFO certification); §404 (internal control reports); §§401(a) (off-balance-sheet disclosure), 402 (loans to executives); §§802, 806, 807, 906, 1102, 1107 (document destruction, whistleblowers, criminal penalties).\n\n**Documents:**\n- `sox-plaw-html`: the section text.\n- `sox-crs-summary`.\n- `sox-srpt-107-205`: purpose and background and the section-by-section parts.\n- `sox-hrpt-107-610`: the conference report's explanations.\n- `sox-hrpt-107-414`: selectively.\n- `sox-pitt-testimony`, `sec-press-2003-52`, `sec-pcaob-101d-order`, `sec-pcaob-103-order`.\n- `sec-sox704-report`: executive summary.\n- `gao-03-864`: summary, only for auditor concentration and rotation.\n- `sox-bush-remarks`, `sox-bush-signing-statement`.\n- The three `sox-hrg-banking-v1/-v2/-v3` volumes: **search only** (grep the text copies for Enron-linked testimony on each provision), then read just the hits. Record page ranges.\n\n**Also:** `work/facts/reader-sox-gaps.md`: anything the page would want that the library lacks, especially what happened **after 2003** (e.g. how §404 was applied, PCAOB Auditing Standards No. 2 and 5, inspections). These go to the Source Scout. Final report as usual.\n\n---\nThis agent was also bound by the common rules for every agent, in work/briefs/00-common-rules.md.",
